WEBVTT

1
00:47:04.098 --> 00:47:09.098
What is so cool is, I have said this before, but God is the best organizer.

2
00:47:09.098 --> 00:47:15.098
I find that so cool. Everything that has been said, both by Robert and by Bram,

3
00:47:15.098 --> 00:47:20.098
and the songs we have sung, everything is in one line.

4
00:47:20.098 --> 00:47:25.098
And that is that the Holy Spirit wants to fill you, that the Holy Spirit wants to change you,

5
00:47:25.098 --> 00:47:29.098
that the Holy Spirit wants to be with you in your life.

6
00:47:29.098 --> 00:47:42.098
And that makes us one. There is one God, one Holy Spirit, one Son, one work of salvation, and one church.

7
00:47:42.098 --> 00:47:46.098
And I don't mean specifically Open Church, I mean one church worldwide,

8
00:47:46.098 --> 00:47:54.098
namely those who confess Jesus Christ as Savior and Redeemer. Amen.

9
00:47:55.098 --> 00:48:04.098
Today we are going to look at what it means to be a temple of the Holy Spirit.

10
00:48:04.098 --> 00:48:11.098
What? What are you saying? That's complicated. What do you mean?

11
00:48:11.098 --> 00:48:19.098
Well, let me put it this way. You yourself are a temple in which God, in which the Holy Spirit wants to dwell.

12
00:48:20.098 --> 00:48:24.098
And that is a bit tricky, that is difficult. What do you mean?

13
00:48:24.098 --> 00:48:30.098
Well, the Bible often speaks with comparisons, with parables, with examples.

14
00:48:30.098 --> 00:48:34.098
Bram just had such an example about a treasure in a field.

15
00:48:34.098 --> 00:48:41.098
And that someone wants to have that treasure and thinks, no matter what happens, I must have that field.

16
00:48:41.098 --> 00:48:46.098
And he puts everything on the line to get that treasure in that field.

17
00:48:46.098 --> 00:48:53.098
Well, that is an example. And it is also an example that you are a temple of the Holy Spirit.

18
00:48:53.098 --> 00:49:01.098
It is literally that the Holy Spirit wants to dwell in you. He really wants to be with you.

19
00:49:01.098 --> 00:49:07.098
And of course, you yourself are the temple. We are like a building.

20
00:49:07.098 --> 00:49:14.098
And you might think, yes but, a building, this is the church, right? Yes, but this is not a temple.

21
00:49:14.098 --> 00:49:18.098
In fact, this building is not a church either.

22
00:49:18.098 --> 00:49:23.098
No, these are just a few walls and a roof on top.

23
00:49:23.098 --> 00:49:28.098
And if things go well, the roof will come off, but this is just a building.

24
00:49:28.098 --> 00:49:35.098
And what we are building, and the construction project is also for an extra building, a new building.

25
00:49:35.098 --> 00:49:41.098
We are not going to build a temple, we are not going to build a church, there will be no rooster standing on it.

26
00:49:42.098 --> 00:49:47.098
It is just a building, because we together are the church.

27
00:49:47.098 --> 00:49:53.098
Imagine, the church in Zonhoven. There, it has burned down.

28
00:49:53.098 --> 00:49:58.098
And then? Yes, then they rent another building and that is where the church is.

29
00:49:58.098 --> 00:50:01.098
So it is not the building where you come together.

30
00:50:01.098 --> 00:50:06.098
Don't get me wrong, I have immense respect for this place.

31
00:50:07.098 --> 00:50:12.098
And when I come here, even during the week, and it is quiet here, and I am all alone.

32
00:50:12.098 --> 00:50:19.098
And I think that Inge, Inge is our queen of cleaning, and she could actually use some help too.

33
00:50:19.098 --> 00:50:25.098
But it is like this, when you are here, during the week, and you are alone here.

34
00:50:25.098 --> 00:50:31.098
Yes, I always find it so nice here.

35
00:50:31.098 --> 00:50:37.098
There is really a blessing here, there is a protection here.

36
00:50:37.098 --> 00:50:40.098
Being here is wonderful.

37
00:50:40.098 --> 00:50:46.098
But if we all were to move, it would still just be a building.

38
00:50:46.098 --> 00:50:51.098
It is also true that the Holy Spirit goes with you and me.

39
00:50:51.098 --> 00:50:55.098
For we ourselves are that church, we ourselves are that temple.

40
00:50:55.098 --> 00:51:00.098
At the end of the service when we all say amen and our coffee is finished and everything, we go home.

41
00:51:00.098 --> 00:51:07.098
Then it is not the case that the Holy Spirit is left here all alone, waiting for us to come back.

42
00:51:07.098 --> 00:51:10.098
No, He goes with us.

43
00:51:10.098 --> 00:51:13.098
He wants to go with you.

44
00:51:13.098 --> 00:51:16.098
And that is what we are going to talk about.

45
00:51:16.098 --> 00:51:20.098
But we are not going to just pull that out of thin air.

46
00:51:20.098 --> 00:51:24.098
That is based on the Bible. So let's take a look.

47
00:51:24.098 --> 00:51:28.098
A beautiful book by Paul, 1 Corinthians 3.

48
00:51:29.098 --> 00:51:33.098
Verse 16. For there it is written.

49
00:51:33.098 --> 00:51:40.098
Do not forget that you are the temple of God and in that temple dwells God's Spirit.

50
00:51:42.098 --> 00:51:46.098
You and I, we are like a building, we are a temple.

51
00:51:46.098 --> 00:51:49.098
And in us, God's Spirit wants to dwell.

52
00:51:52.098 --> 00:51:57.098
If you let that sink in for a moment, that is really quite intense.

53
00:51:58.098 --> 00:52:03.098
Because we as humans think, yes, up there somewhere, there is God.

54
00:52:05.098 --> 00:52:08.098
And then His Spirit wants to be in you.

55
00:52:08.098 --> 00:52:11.098
How is that possible? In me.

56
00:52:12.098 --> 00:52:16.098
I am not doing everything right and I am not perfect enough,

57
00:52:16.098 --> 00:52:19.098
so that Spirit could dwell in me.

58
00:52:21.098 --> 00:52:24.098
But that is exactly how He will help you.

59
00:52:25.098 --> 00:52:29.098
1 Corinthians 3, verse 16, that was.

60
00:52:29.098 --> 00:52:35.098
Do not forget that you are the temple of God and in that temple dwells God's Spirit.

61
00:52:37.098 --> 00:52:40.098
I will go back a little to verse 9.

62
00:52:40.098 --> 00:52:44.098
You could also say, you are God's building.

63
00:52:44.098 --> 00:52:48.098
Paul is a wonderful teacher.

64
00:52:48.098 --> 00:52:53.098
And if you only take one sentence out of it, you might still think,

65
00:52:53.098 --> 00:52:56.098
well, how so?

66
00:52:56.098 --> 00:53:01.098
And that is why it is always good to read the Bible, and even if you have a verse of the day,

67
00:53:01.098 --> 00:53:07.098
to still grab your Bible and look a few verses back and a few verses forward.

68
00:53:07.098 --> 00:53:10.098
For especially Paul explains things so beautifully.

69
00:53:10.098 --> 00:53:12.098
So back to verse 9.

70
00:53:12.098 --> 00:53:15.098
You could say, you are God's building.

71
00:53:15.098 --> 00:53:18.098
We have talked about that before.

72
00:53:19.098 --> 00:53:20.098
Verse 11.

73
00:53:20.098 --> 00:53:25.098
No one may lay another foundation than the one that is already laid.

74
00:53:25.098 --> 00:53:29.098
For that foundation is Jesus Christ.

75
00:53:29.098 --> 00:53:36.098
Later it will become clear how everyone has built further on this foundation.

76
00:53:36.098 --> 00:53:39.098
I will linger here for a moment.

77
00:53:39.098 --> 00:53:42.098
The foundation is Jesus Christ.

78
00:53:42.098 --> 00:53:44.098
That is our basis.

79
00:53:44.098 --> 00:53:46.098
That is what we build our lives on.

80
00:53:46.098 --> 00:53:47.098
That is what we base our lives on.

81
00:53:47.098 --> 00:53:49.098
We base our choices on that.

82
00:53:49.098 --> 00:53:53.098
We base how we look at others on that.

83
00:53:53.098 --> 00:53:56.098
Love God and love people.

84
00:53:56.098 --> 00:53:58.098
That is what Jesus said.

85
00:53:58.098 --> 00:54:00.098
We base our lives on that.

86
00:54:00.098 --> 00:54:03.098
Those are our norms and values.

87
00:54:03.098 --> 00:54:06.098
Let's continue. Verse 11.

88
00:54:06.098 --> 00:54:13.098
If you have built well, that can be compared to gold, silver, and precious stones.

89
00:54:13.098 --> 00:54:22.098
If you build poorly, that can be compared to wood, hay, and straw.

90
00:54:22.098 --> 00:54:25.098
That is quite clear.

91
00:54:27.098 --> 00:54:28.098
Verse 16.

92
00:54:28.098 --> 00:54:35.098
Do not forget that you are the temple of God and in that temple dwells God's spirit.

93
00:54:35.098 --> 00:54:40.098
We are talking here about an imaginary building, of course.

94
00:54:40.098 --> 00:54:43.098
We sometimes say building your house of life.

95
00:54:43.098 --> 00:54:46.098
That simply means, how do you organize your life?

96
00:54:46.098 --> 00:54:48.098
What do you find important?

97
00:54:48.098 --> 00:54:50.098
What are your principles?

98
00:54:50.098 --> 00:54:51.098
What is your foundation?

99
00:54:51.098 --> 00:54:53.098
We have already talked about the foundation.

100
00:54:53.098 --> 00:54:55.098
That is Jesus.

101
00:54:55.098 --> 00:54:57.098
That is the Word of God.

102
00:55:00.098 --> 00:55:01.098
Should you do that?

103
00:55:01.098 --> 00:55:02.098
No, that should not be done.

104
00:55:02.098 --> 00:55:03.098
You should decide for yourself.

105
00:55:03.098 --> 00:55:05.098
That is your own choice.

106
00:55:05.098 --> 00:55:10.098
But if you want to build well, as Paul says here,

107
00:55:10.098 --> 00:55:16.098
whoever builds well builds with gold, silver, and precious stones.

108
00:55:17.098 --> 00:55:21.098
And whoever does not build well, builds with wood, hay, and straw.

109
00:55:22.098 --> 00:55:27.098
I always think, I am visually oriented, so I always think,

110
00:55:27.098 --> 00:55:31.098
okay, a temple of the Holy Spirit, what does that look like?

111
00:55:31.098 --> 00:55:33.098
I create a picture in my mind.

112
00:55:33.098 --> 00:55:35.098
What picture do you have in your head?

113
00:55:35.098 --> 00:55:38.098
For me, it is very beautiful white marble.

114
00:55:39.098 --> 00:55:45.098
White marble, finished with gold, with precious stones in the doorposts.

115
00:55:45.098 --> 00:55:47.098
Completely beautifully finished.

116
00:55:47.098 --> 00:55:49.098
That's how I envision it.

117
00:55:50.098 --> 00:55:53.098
But the question is, what is the difference?

118
00:55:53.098 --> 00:55:59.098
What is the difference when you build well and what is the difference when you build poorly?

119
00:55:59.098 --> 00:56:00.098
What do you do then?

120
00:56:00.098 --> 00:56:05.098
What is the difference in daily life between building well and building poorly?

121
00:56:05.098 --> 00:56:06.098
How then?

122
00:56:06.098 --> 00:56:09.098
Because this is all such a comparison.

123
00:56:09.098 --> 00:56:14.098
And this may not be so practical to grasp for what you should do in your daily life.

124
00:56:14.098 --> 00:56:16.098
So let's take a look at that.

125
00:56:18.098 --> 00:56:25.098
I imagine, when Paul says good building is with gold and precious stones,

126
00:56:25.098 --> 00:56:27.098
and I then think of white marble,

127
00:56:27.098 --> 00:56:32.098
then I also think, what does it look like when you build wrong or poorly?

128
00:56:32.098 --> 00:56:34.098
With wood and hay.

129
00:56:34.098 --> 00:56:38.098
Yes, I then see a very rickety little hut in front of me,

130
00:56:38.098 --> 00:56:44.098
with a bit of mud and also not drawn by an architect,

131
00:56:44.098 --> 00:56:46.098
but just a bit thrown together.

132
00:56:46.098 --> 00:56:47.098
You know?

133
00:56:47.098 --> 00:56:51.098
Something that you might have standing way back in your garden,

134
00:56:51.098 --> 00:56:52.098
for the chickens or something.

135
00:56:52.098 --> 00:56:53.098
You know?

136
00:56:53.098 --> 00:56:56.098
And what just collapses after a while.

137
00:56:56.098 --> 00:56:58.098
I visualize that.

138
00:56:58.098 --> 00:57:02.098
And some time ago I already spoke about this,

139
00:57:02.098 --> 00:57:05.098
about renovating your house of life.

140
00:57:05.098 --> 00:57:06.098
Do you remember?

141
00:57:06.098 --> 00:57:09.098
Clutter out, love in.

142
00:57:09.098 --> 00:57:12.098
And Caroline has sung just as clearly about that too,

143
00:57:12.098 --> 00:57:14.098
from here fill me with your love.

144
00:57:14.098 --> 00:57:18.098
That clutter that you sometimes drag along in your life,

145
00:57:18.098 --> 00:57:20.098
you need to throw it out.

146
00:57:20.098 --> 00:57:22.098
Settle accounts with the clutter.

147
00:57:22.098 --> 00:57:25.098
And ask for God's love in your life.

148
00:57:26.098 --> 00:57:30.098
It's not just the things that you do wrong yourself,

149
00:57:30.098 --> 00:57:33.098
but also the injustice that has been done to you.

150
00:57:33.098 --> 00:57:36.098
Vanessa spoke about that last week.

151
00:57:36.098 --> 00:57:39.098
Sometimes you also do injustice to others yourself.

152
00:57:39.098 --> 00:57:42.098
Then the blame is simply on you.

153
00:57:42.098 --> 00:57:45.098
And you might carry those debts with you your whole life.

154
00:57:45.098 --> 00:57:47.098
But you can settle accounts with that.

155
00:57:47.098 --> 00:57:49.098
You can put a line under it.

156
00:57:49.098 --> 00:57:52.098
And the injustice that has been done to you,

157
00:57:53.098 --> 00:57:57.098
that can cause not only pain or insecurity,

158
00:57:57.098 --> 00:58:00.098
but also bitterness, anger.

159
00:58:00.098 --> 00:58:02.098
You can put a line under that.

160
00:58:02.098 --> 00:58:04.098
You can settle accounts with that.

161
00:58:04.098 --> 00:58:06.098
You can say that, done.

162
00:58:06.098 --> 00:58:09.098
And that’s what I meant last time with,

163
00:58:09.098 --> 00:58:11.098
junk out, love in.

164
00:58:11.098 --> 00:58:13.098
Deal with those things.

165
00:58:13.098 --> 00:58:15.098
Draw a line under it.

166
00:58:16.098 --> 00:58:20.098
And God is so loving, because He just wants to help you with that.

167
00:58:21.098 --> 00:58:23.098
He wants the best for you.

168
00:58:23.098 --> 00:58:27.098
He wants plan A, A, A plus for you.

169
00:58:28.098 --> 00:58:30.098
Not plan B.

170
00:58:30.098 --> 00:58:32.098
He wants the best for you.

171
00:58:32.098 --> 00:58:35.098
But okay, you might say.

172
00:58:35.098 --> 00:58:37.098
We have done that.

173
00:58:37.098 --> 00:58:38.098
The junk is out.

174
00:58:38.098 --> 00:58:40.098
The love is in.

175
00:58:40.098 --> 00:58:42.098
I have come to faith.

176
00:58:42.098 --> 00:58:47.098
I have decided, I want Jesus as the foundation in my life.

177
00:58:47.098 --> 00:58:50.098
On that basis, I want to continue building.

178
00:58:50.098 --> 00:58:52.098
What then?

179
00:58:52.098 --> 00:58:54.098
How do you continue building?

180
00:58:55.098 --> 00:58:58.098
There is only one thing, and that is the Holy Spirit.

181
00:58:58.098 --> 00:59:00.098
You need that.

182
00:59:00.098 --> 00:59:02.098
First you say to Jesus,

183
00:59:02.098 --> 00:59:05.098
yes, I accept you into my life.

184
00:59:05.098 --> 00:59:08.098
I take on what you have done for me.

185
00:59:08.098 --> 00:59:10.098
You are my savior.

186
00:59:10.098 --> 00:59:12.098
Wash me clean.

187
00:59:12.098 --> 00:59:15.098
Erase all the mess in my life.

188
00:59:15.098 --> 00:59:18.098
And I make a new decision and a new start.

189
00:59:18.098 --> 00:59:20.098
That is step one.

190
00:59:20.098 --> 00:59:23.098
And then you need the Holy Spirit.

191
00:59:24.098 --> 00:59:27.098
It cannot be that you get baptized.

192
00:59:27.098 --> 00:59:29.098
Tim said that last week too.

193
00:59:29.098 --> 00:59:32.098
That you get baptized and say, okay, now I'm done.

194
00:59:32.098 --> 00:59:34.098
Finished.

195
00:59:34.098 --> 00:59:39.098
No, because it is very clear that Paul speaks about building your house of life.

196
00:59:39.098 --> 00:59:46.098
And it is also not that after your baptism you immediately fall over, die.

197
00:59:46.098 --> 00:59:48.098
And then it's done.

198
00:59:48.098 --> 00:59:50.098
No, you continue with your life.

199
00:59:50.098 --> 00:59:52.098
So you build your life further.

200
00:59:52.098 --> 00:59:54.098
So how do we do that?

201
00:59:54.098 --> 00:59:57.098
Well, I always compare it like this.

202
00:59:57.098 --> 01:00:00.098
You also just have to clean your own house.

203
01:00:00.098 --> 01:00:02.098
Every week.

204
01:00:03.098 --> 01:00:07.098
If you don't do that, the spiders will crawl over the windowsill.

205
01:00:08.098 --> 01:00:11.098
Or the spider webs will hang from the ceiling.

206
01:00:13.098 --> 01:00:16.098
And so it is with your house or your apartment.

207
01:00:16.098 --> 01:00:19.098
You have to clean it, you have to mop, you have to wash the windows.

208
01:00:19.098 --> 01:00:22.098
Otherwise, soon you won't be able to see through the window.

209
01:00:23.098 --> 01:00:26.098
And it is the same with your life house.

210
01:00:27.098 --> 01:00:29.098
You have to keep maintaining it.

211
01:00:29.098 --> 01:00:33.098
You can't just say once, I'll sweep through it and that's it.

212
01:00:33.098 --> 01:00:36.098
Every day you have to maintain it.

213
01:00:37.098 --> 01:00:40.098
Every day you have to look at your behavior.

214
01:00:42.098 --> 01:00:44.098
At your character.

215
01:00:45.098 --> 01:00:47.098
At your way of reacting.

216
01:00:47.098 --> 01:00:50.098
To what you did that day.

217
01:00:50.098 --> 01:00:54.098
And that actually means, the Word is self-reflection.

218
01:00:55.098 --> 01:00:58.098
You look at yourself at the end of the day.

219
01:00:58.098 --> 01:01:00.098
At the end of the day.

220
01:01:00.098 --> 01:01:04.098
And you actually go to what you did that day.

221
01:01:04.098 --> 01:01:07.098
And especially the difficult moments.

222
01:01:07.098 --> 01:01:09.098
That awful conversation you had at work.

223
01:01:09.098 --> 01:01:14.098
Or that clash with the neighbors over their barking dog.

224
01:01:14.098 --> 01:01:15.098
And things like that.

225
01:01:15.098 --> 01:01:18.098
Then you just apply self-reflection.

226
01:01:18.098 --> 01:01:20.098
But I have a new word.

227
01:01:20.098 --> 01:01:22.098
New word of the week.

228
01:01:22.098 --> 01:01:24.098
Holy Spirit reflection.

229
01:01:25.098 --> 01:01:28.098
Because when you apply self-reflection.

230
01:01:29.098 --> 01:01:31.098
What is then the norm?

231
01:01:33.098 --> 01:01:35.098
What is then the value?

232
01:01:36.098 --> 01:01:38.098
Do you determine that yourself?

233
01:01:39.098 --> 01:01:41.098
Or do you say no, Holy Spirit.

234
01:01:41.098 --> 01:01:42.098
Come to me.

235
01:01:42.098 --> 01:01:43.098
Fill me.

236
01:01:44.098 --> 01:01:46.098
And at the end of the day, Holy Spirit.

237
01:01:46.098 --> 01:01:47.098
I'm just going to.

238
01:01:48.098 --> 01:01:49.098
I'm lying in my bed.

239
01:01:49.098 --> 01:01:51.098
Before I fall asleep.

240
01:01:51.098 --> 01:01:52.098
Holy Spirit.

241
01:01:52.098 --> 01:01:54.098
I want to first go through the day.

242
01:01:54.098 --> 01:01:56.098
How did it go for me today?

243
01:01:58.098 --> 01:02:00.098
And the Holy Spirit indicates.

244
01:02:02.098 --> 01:02:04.098
That wasn't so great.

245
01:02:04.098 --> 01:02:06.098
Or you should pay attention to that.

246
01:02:07.098 --> 01:02:10.098
And that is actually Holy Spirit reflection.

247
01:02:10.098 --> 01:02:14.098
He takes you on the foundation of Jesus Christ.

248
01:02:14.098 --> 01:02:16.098
On the standards of Jesus Christ.

249
01:02:21.098 --> 01:02:25.098
It is indeed the Holy Spirit who convinces of sin.

250
01:02:25.098 --> 01:02:26.098
Says the Bible.

251
01:02:28.098 --> 01:02:30.098
So if you have done something wrong.

252
01:02:30.098 --> 01:02:33.098
But you don't think about it in the evening.

253
01:02:33.098 --> 01:02:37.098
You don't ask the Holy Spirit to take a look with you.

254
01:02:38.098 --> 01:02:41.098
The Holy Spirit convinces of sin.

255
01:02:41.098 --> 01:02:44.098
There, what you did there, that was not right.

256
01:02:45.098 --> 01:02:47.098
And that is building.

257
01:02:47.098 --> 01:02:49.098
What is building your life house?

258
01:02:49.098 --> 01:02:51.098
Do you make mistakes? Yes.

259
01:02:51.098 --> 01:02:53.098
But the Holy Spirit then says.

260
01:02:53.098 --> 01:02:55.098
Hey, that was not good.

261
01:02:55.098 --> 01:02:57.098
And then you can change that.

262
01:02:57.098 --> 01:03:02.098
Then you can take that wood that you used that day.

263
01:03:03.098 --> 01:03:05.098
You only used it that day.

264
01:03:05.098 --> 01:03:07.098
You can easily remove it.

265
01:03:07.098 --> 01:03:08.098
And then the Holy Spirit says.

266
01:03:08.098 --> 01:03:10.098
Yes, but I will help you.

267
01:03:10.098 --> 01:03:12.098
So that it becomes something beautiful.

268
01:03:12.098 --> 01:03:14.098
That it gets transformed.

269
01:03:14.098 --> 01:03:16.098
We are going to change that.

270
01:03:17.098 --> 01:03:19.098
And then you think.

271
01:03:19.098 --> 01:03:21.098
Yes, but how then?

272
01:03:21.098 --> 01:03:23.098
I don't sin anymore, do I?

273
01:03:23.098 --> 01:03:25.098
I have Jesus' forgiveness, right?

274
01:03:25.098 --> 01:03:27.098
I don't do anything wrong anymore, do I?

275
01:03:27.098 --> 01:03:30.098
Yes, maybe not.

276
01:03:30.098 --> 01:03:35.098
But the world around us clings to us.

277
01:03:36.098 --> 01:03:40.098
Every day you at least step outside the door.

278
01:03:40.098 --> 01:03:42.098
And if you don't go outside the door.

279
01:03:42.098 --> 01:03:44.098
The world still comes into your house.

280
01:03:44.098 --> 01:03:46.098
Through social media.

281
01:03:46.098 --> 01:03:47.098
Or through the TV.

282
01:03:47.098 --> 01:03:48.098
Or the newspaper.

283
01:03:48.098 --> 01:03:52.098
Or what family members might bring along.

284
01:03:52.098 --> 01:03:53.098
And bring.

285
01:03:53.098 --> 01:03:54.098
And tell.

286
01:03:54.098 --> 01:03:55.098
Or whatever.

287
01:03:55.098 --> 01:03:58.098
So the world around us clings to us.

288
01:03:58.098 --> 01:04:03.098
And what you might have dealt with.

289
01:04:03.098 --> 01:04:05.098
In the baptismal water.

290
01:04:05.098 --> 01:04:07.098
Those old habits.

291
01:04:07.098 --> 01:04:10.098
They will still come after you.

292
01:04:11.098 --> 01:04:16.098
By yourself, you might manage to behave nicely for two or three weeks.

293
01:04:16.098 --> 01:04:20.098
But ultimately, you can't maintain that if it's from yourself.

294
01:04:20.098 --> 01:04:23.098
And those habits will come after you again.

295
01:04:23.098 --> 01:04:27.098
And they want to catch you by the collar again.

296
01:04:27.098 --> 01:04:31.098
And so there are things from the world.

297
01:04:31.098 --> 01:04:33.098
That are simply around you.

298
01:04:33.098 --> 01:04:35.098
And that stick to you.

299
01:04:36.098 --> 01:04:42.098
It's not just three weeks of hurray hurray hallelujah.

300
01:04:42.098 --> 01:04:44.098
And then.

301
01:04:44.098 --> 01:04:46.098
And then.

302
01:04:46.098 --> 01:04:48.098
No.

303
01:04:48.098 --> 01:04:50.098
Try to hold on.

304
01:04:50.098 --> 01:04:51.098
Hang in there.

305
01:04:51.098 --> 01:04:52.098
Do your best.

306
01:04:52.098 --> 01:04:54.098
Why do I have to do my best?

307
01:04:54.098 --> 01:04:55.098
Yes.

308
01:04:55.098 --> 01:04:57.098
Because it is your own choice.

309
01:04:57.098 --> 01:05:02.098
It's not like you're completely in a haze.

310
01:05:02.098 --> 01:05:04.098
And that everything just happens automatically.

311
01:05:04.098 --> 01:05:06.098
No, it's your own choice.

312
01:05:06.098 --> 01:05:08.098
Coming to faith is your own choice.

313
01:05:08.098 --> 01:05:12.098
Inviting the Holy Spirit into your life is your own choice.

314
01:05:12.098 --> 01:05:14.098
And then continue.

315
01:05:14.098 --> 01:05:15.098
Step by step.

316
01:05:15.098 --> 01:05:17.098
Is your own choice.

317
01:05:18.098 --> 01:05:21.098
How did it go for me today, Holy Spirit?

318
01:05:21.098 --> 01:05:23.098
I had a party.

319
01:05:23.098 --> 01:05:25.098
And I was at work.

320
01:05:25.098 --> 01:05:29.098
And I did have a rough moment somewhere.

321
01:05:29.098 --> 01:05:32.098
I had a silly conversation with someone.

322
01:05:33.098 --> 01:05:35.098
What is on my mind?

323
01:05:35.098 --> 01:05:39.098
And the Holy Spirit, He guides you through that.

324
01:05:39.098 --> 01:05:44.098
He shows you where you need to pay attention.

325
01:05:44.098 --> 01:05:46.098
What can still be just a little bit better.

326
01:05:46.098 --> 01:05:51.098
And so you actually move forward step by step.

327
01:05:51.098 --> 01:05:53.098
And you build your house.

328
01:05:54.098 --> 01:06:03.098
Have you ever had it that a joke is told at your work?

329
01:06:03.098 --> 01:06:07.098
Where you actually have to laugh.

330
01:06:07.098 --> 01:06:12.098
But you really hear it in your head, in your heart.

331
01:06:12.098 --> 01:06:13.098
The Holy Spirit says.

332
01:06:13.098 --> 01:06:15.098
Hey, that really can't be, can it?

333
01:06:15.098 --> 01:06:17.098
You just can't laugh at this.

334
01:06:17.098 --> 01:06:19.098
Yes, but it's so funny.

335
01:06:20.098 --> 01:06:24.098
No, that's exactly the Holy Spirit reflection.

336
01:06:24.098 --> 01:06:26.098
The Holy Spirit indicating that.

337
01:06:26.098 --> 01:06:28.098
Yes, but this can't be.

338
01:06:28.098 --> 01:06:29.098
You need to change this.

339
01:06:29.098 --> 01:06:33.098
Or what do you think about boundary-pushing videos?

340
01:06:33.098 --> 01:06:34.098
Or movies?

341
01:06:34.098 --> 01:06:37.098
When you're watching a movie and then think.

342
01:06:39.098 --> 01:06:41.098
Yes, it's Saturday night.

343
01:06:41.098 --> 01:06:44.098
Well, tomorrow I have to go to the service.

344
01:06:44.098 --> 01:06:47.098
Actually, those two can't go together, the movie and the service.

345
01:06:47.098 --> 01:06:48.098
That's not a combination.

346
01:06:48.098 --> 01:06:51.098
Yes, that's boundary-pushing.

347
01:06:51.098 --> 01:06:55.098
I remember very well in the early nineties.

348
01:06:55.098 --> 01:06:57.098
That a number of films were released.

349
01:06:57.098 --> 01:07:02.098
I'm not going to name topics, but you can think of them yourself.

350
01:07:02.098 --> 01:07:08.098
Of which it was the first time that it was shown in a film.

351
01:07:08.098 --> 01:07:10.098
And we really had something like.

352
01:07:10.098 --> 01:07:13.098
Wow, oh, I really can't watch that.

353
01:07:13.098 --> 01:07:14.098
Oh, I'll skip that part.

354
01:07:14.098 --> 01:07:15.098
Or I'll turn it off.

355
01:07:15.098 --> 01:07:18.098
And now we're thirty years later.

356
01:07:18.098 --> 01:07:21.098
And we actually think something like.

357
01:07:21.098 --> 01:07:24.098
Yes, that's the world, that's what you have.

358
01:07:24.098 --> 01:07:26.098
That happens.

359
01:07:26.098 --> 01:07:29.098
Yes, I know that happens too.

360
01:07:29.098 --> 01:07:32.098
But that doesn't mean I have to pollute my eyes with it.

361
01:07:32.098 --> 01:07:36.098
That I have to pollute my spirit with that.

362
01:07:36.098 --> 01:07:39.098
Because every time you watch that.

363
01:07:39.098 --> 01:07:42.098
Every time you agree to that.

364
01:07:42.098 --> 01:07:46.098
You shift your boundaries of your norms and values.

365
01:07:48.098 --> 01:07:50.098
There are series.

366
01:07:50.098 --> 01:07:53.098
Where if there is a certain topic in it.

367
01:07:53.098 --> 01:07:55.098
A series that we like to follow.

368
01:07:55.098 --> 01:07:56.098
Something simple, something fun.

369
01:07:56.098 --> 01:07:59.098
But if there is a specific topic in it.

370
01:07:59.098 --> 01:08:01.098
We skip that episode.

371
01:08:01.098 --> 01:08:06.098
Because I do not want to compromise my norms and values.

372
01:08:06.098 --> 01:08:09.098
I know very well what happens outside the door.

373
01:08:09.098 --> 01:08:11.098
I really know that.

374
01:08:11.098 --> 01:08:16.098
But that doesn't mean I have to engage with it.

375
01:08:18.098 --> 01:08:21.098
These are my norms and values.

376
01:08:21.098 --> 01:08:25.098
And you can say, yes but Debbie that goes too far, right?

377
01:08:25.098 --> 01:08:29.098
That you skip series or fast forward episodes.

378
01:08:29.098 --> 01:08:31.098
Yes and?

379
01:08:31.098 --> 01:08:33.098
Yes and?

380
01:08:34.098 --> 01:08:38.098
Do you become worse off by skipping an episode?

381
01:08:38.098 --> 01:08:40.098
Who cares?

382
01:08:40.098 --> 01:08:47.098
But you will be worse off if you blur your norms and values.

383
01:08:47.098 --> 01:08:50.098
That will make you worse off.

384
01:08:50.098 --> 01:08:52.098
And I don't want that.

385
01:08:52.098 --> 01:08:54.098
I do not want that.

386
01:08:57.098 --> 01:08:59.098
What does the Bible say about it further?

387
01:08:59.098 --> 01:09:02.098
Let's take a look in Ephesians 4.

388
01:09:03.098 --> 01:09:06.098
For those who are also taking notes.

389
01:09:06.098 --> 01:09:09.098
Ephesians 4 verses 17 to 32.

390
01:09:09.098 --> 01:09:11.098
Super beautiful piece.

391
01:09:11.098 --> 01:09:14.098
Explains all of this very nicely.

392
01:09:14.098 --> 01:09:17.098
I will only take out a few verses.

393
01:09:17.098 --> 01:09:20.098
But if you want to look further into this.

394
01:09:20.098 --> 01:09:25.098
Next week is Ephesians 4 verses 17 to 32.

395
01:09:25.098 --> 01:09:27.098
I recommend it to you.

396
01:09:28.098 --> 01:09:36.098
So what does Paul say about this whole thing, about Holy Spirit reflection?

397
01:09:36.098 --> 01:09:41.098
That word didn't exist back then, but the theme is the same.

398
01:09:41.098 --> 01:09:43.098
Verse 17.

399
01:09:43.098 --> 01:09:52.098
I tell you on behalf of the Lord that you must no longer live as the unbelieving people do.

400
01:09:53.098 --> 01:10:00.098
For they devise meaningless, boundary-pushing things.

401
01:10:00.098 --> 01:10:03.098
We just shouldn't think the same way.

402
01:10:03.098 --> 01:10:05.098
Then we shouldn't look the same way either.

403
01:10:05.098 --> 01:10:07.098
Then we shouldn't listen the same way either.

404
01:10:07.098 --> 01:10:10.098
Then we shouldn't laugh at the same jokes either.

405
01:10:11.098 --> 01:10:13.098
Verse 20.

406
01:10:13.098 --> 01:10:15.098
But you must be completely different.

407
01:10:15.098 --> 01:10:18.098
For you have come to know Christ.

408
01:10:18.098 --> 01:10:21.098
You have the foundation of Christ.

409
01:10:21.098 --> 01:10:22.098
Verse 23.

410
01:10:22.098 --> 01:10:30.098
But now you can change your life by a new way of thinking.

411
01:10:31.098 --> 01:10:33.098
And that is it.

412
01:10:33.098 --> 01:10:37.098
So well described, Paul. Yes, I really like that.

413
01:10:39.098 --> 01:10:41.098
So what does it say here, what does Paul say?

414
01:10:41.098 --> 01:10:44.098
We need to learn to think in a new way.

415
01:10:44.098 --> 01:10:48.098
We should no longer think the way we used to.

416
01:10:48.098 --> 01:10:53.098
We shouldn't think like our neighbors or family or colleagues do, or classmates.

417
01:10:53.098 --> 01:10:55.098
No, we think in a different way.

418
01:10:55.098 --> 01:10:58.098
And that is of course logical, because it is based on the Bible.

419
01:11:05.098 --> 01:11:09.098
Back to the house and the building.

420
01:11:09.098 --> 01:11:15.098
You can't imagine being here on Sunday and building something very beautiful.

421
01:11:16.098 --> 01:11:19.098
And you learn certain things here.

422
01:11:19.098 --> 01:11:24.098
And you build with marble and beautifully finished with gold.

423
01:11:24.098 --> 01:11:27.098
That is on Sunday.

424
01:11:27.098 --> 01:11:32.098
But then on Monday through Saturday, we forget that.

425
01:11:32.098 --> 01:11:35.098
And then we continue in our own way.

426
01:11:36.098 --> 01:11:39.098
And then we build with wood and straw.

427
01:11:39.098 --> 01:11:44.098
But think for a moment, what a strange structure that will be.

428
01:11:44.098 --> 01:11:48.098
And then you come back on Sunday and continue with gold.

429
01:11:48.098 --> 01:11:53.098
Are you going to pour that gold over the straw or...

430
01:11:53.098 --> 01:11:59.098
then you have finished with gold and gemstones among the hay.

431
01:11:59.098 --> 01:12:01.098
What?

432
01:12:01.098 --> 01:12:05.098
Then there is marble on top and a wooden slat.

433
01:12:06.098 --> 01:12:09.098
You can already feel that it will collapse.

434
01:12:09.098 --> 01:12:12.098
That is unstable. It doesn't work that way.

435
01:12:12.098 --> 01:12:16.098
That doesn't work. It will collapse. That is unstable.

436
01:12:16.098 --> 01:12:20.098
Then nothing beautiful will ever come out of it, ultimately.

437
01:12:20.098 --> 01:12:23.098
God is our builder. He is the architect.

438
01:12:23.098 --> 01:12:26.098
And He has a plan for each of us.

439
01:12:26.098 --> 01:12:28.098
A life plan.

440
01:12:28.098 --> 01:12:30.098
Who you are, because you are unique.

441
01:12:30.098 --> 01:12:35.098
With your own character, with your own insights, with your own mission in life.

442
01:12:35.098 --> 01:12:39.098
You are unique. And that builder, that is God.

443
01:12:40.098 --> 01:12:43.098
And this is the building plan.

444
01:12:48.098 --> 01:12:54.098
You know, you cannot continue to hold on to the old way of thinking, as Paul speaks about this,

445
01:12:54.098 --> 01:13:00.098
while also adopting the new way of thinking.

446
01:13:00.098 --> 01:13:03.098
At the same time. That doesn't work. Tim has demonstrated this as well.

447
01:13:03.098 --> 01:13:08.098
You cannot have one foot in the world and one foot in the church.

448
01:13:08.098 --> 01:13:15.098
Living roughly with one foot and with the other foot saying, I am doing so well.

449
01:13:15.098 --> 01:13:17.098
That doesn't work like that.

450
01:13:17.098 --> 01:13:19.098
Yes, but I am a good person, right?

451
01:13:19.098 --> 01:13:23.098
Yes, nice, but that is not enough.

452
01:13:23.098 --> 01:13:27.098
We need God. We need the Holy Spirit in our lives.

453
01:13:27.098 --> 01:13:31.098
And that is why that Holy Spirit reflection is so important.

454
01:13:31.098 --> 01:13:36.098
Help me, Holy Spirit, to see a new way of thinking.

455
01:13:36.098 --> 01:13:39.098
To think in a new way.

456
01:13:39.098 --> 01:13:44.098
I want to leave the old way of thinking and doing behind me.

457
01:13:44.098 --> 01:13:52.098
And you know, it doesn't matter if you are here for the first time, or the first month,

458
01:13:52.098 --> 01:13:57.098
or if you have just been baptized recently, or if you have been here for thirty years.

459
01:13:58.098 --> 01:14:03.098
That doesn't matter, because life around us continues to be around us.

460
01:14:04.098 --> 01:14:13.098
And to be honest, in the last thirty years, the thinking outside in the world has only become stranger.

461
01:14:13.098 --> 01:14:19.098
So you can't say, yes but then I came to faith, so I'm doing well.

462
01:14:19.098 --> 01:14:21.098
And I am a good person and I do good things.

463
01:14:21.098 --> 01:14:25.098
No, we need the Holy Spirit every day.

464
01:14:25.098 --> 01:14:30.098
Every day we must think and apply Holy Spirit reflection.

465
01:14:30.098 --> 01:14:33.098
And say, oh Lord, how is it then?

466
01:14:36.098 --> 01:14:38.098
Old thinking, new thinking.

467
01:14:39.098 --> 01:14:41.098
Paul has something beautiful to say about that.

468
01:14:41.098 --> 01:14:44.098
Just look, in Galatians 5, verse 19.

469
01:14:53.098 --> 01:14:58.098
First we read in this passage from Paul about old thinking.

470
01:14:58.098 --> 01:15:01.098
And then we will read a bit about new thinking.

471
01:15:01.098 --> 01:15:03.098
In the same chapter.

472
01:15:04.098 --> 01:15:08.098
19. It is clear what the desires of the flesh are.

473
01:15:08.098 --> 01:15:12.098
So I actually want to say, you on the foundation.

474
01:15:12.098 --> 01:15:18.098
Self-reflection. I build my foundation, instead of Jesus being the foundation.

475
01:15:18.098 --> 01:15:21.098
It is clear what the desires of the flesh are.

476
01:15:21.098 --> 01:15:25.098
Doing wrong things in the area of sex.

477
01:15:25.098 --> 01:15:27.098
Living recklessly.

478
01:15:28.098 --> 01:15:30.098
Worshiping idols.

479
01:15:30.098 --> 01:15:32.098
Witchcraft.

480
01:15:32.098 --> 01:15:33.098
Hatred.

481
01:15:33.098 --> 01:15:34.098
Quarrel.

482
01:15:34.098 --> 01:15:36.098
Jealousy.

483
01:15:36.098 --> 01:15:38.098
Outbursts of anger.

484
01:15:38.098 --> 01:15:40.098
Selfishness.

485
01:15:40.098 --> 01:15:42.098
Division.

486
01:15:42.098 --> 01:15:44.098
Anger.

487
01:15:44.098 --> 01:15:45.098
Murder.

488
01:15:45.098 --> 01:15:47.098
Drunkenness.

489
01:15:47.098 --> 01:15:49.098
Wild parties.

490
01:15:49.098 --> 01:15:51.098
And more of that sort of thing.

491
01:15:52.098 --> 01:15:54.098
Wow, Paul.

492
01:15:54.098 --> 01:15:56.098
That's quite a list you mention there.

493
01:15:56.098 --> 01:15:58.098
I don't really like that.

494
01:15:58.098 --> 01:16:01.098
It hurts to talk about that.

495
01:16:01.098 --> 01:16:08.098
Paul says, I warn you about this as I have done before.

496
01:16:08.098 --> 01:16:14.098
For those who continue to do these things will not inherit the kingdom of God.

497
01:16:15.098 --> 01:16:17.098
If you then look at verse 20.

498
01:16:18.098 --> 01:16:20.098
All those things he mentions.

499
01:16:20.098 --> 01:16:22.098
Then you think, wow.

500
01:16:22.098 --> 01:16:24.098
Yes, but.

501
01:16:24.098 --> 01:16:26.098
I do not do that.

502
01:16:26.098 --> 01:16:28.098
I do not murder.

503
01:16:28.098 --> 01:16:30.098
I do not worship idols.

504
01:16:30.098 --> 01:16:32.098
I do not practice witchcraft.

505
01:16:32.098 --> 01:16:34.098
No, I do not do any of that.

506
01:16:34.098 --> 01:16:36.098
But you know.

507
01:16:36.098 --> 01:16:40.098
With that, you trivialize the Holy Spirit.

508
01:16:40.098 --> 01:16:42.098
And His voice in you.

509
01:16:42.098 --> 01:16:44.098
When you say.

510
01:16:44.098 --> 01:16:46.098
Yes, I am not jealous either.

511
01:16:47.098 --> 01:16:49.098
Oh yes.

512
01:16:49.098 --> 01:16:51.098
Did you laugh or make comments.

513
01:16:51.098 --> 01:16:54.098
About that fancy car of your boss or your manager.

514
01:16:55.098 --> 01:16:57.098
That is actually jealousy too.

515
01:16:57.098 --> 01:17:00.098
Just let that man drive that nice car.

516
01:17:00.098 --> 01:17:03.098
You have no idea how much he has to bend over backwards.

